## Milestone specification

````markdown
## Approved UI Navigation & Project-Centric Structure Refactoring — 2026-10-18

On 2026-10-18 the user approved Milestone M99 through `memory-bank-propose` and `/plan`. This work refactors the Web UI navigation to be project-centric, provides top-level switching between Projects and Artifacts, streamlines project creation with working directory context, and cleans up command categorization.

**Goal.**
1. Sidebar top dual tabs: Place two tabs on the left sidebar: `PROJECTS` (default) and `ARTIFACTS`.
2. Project selection dropdown: Include `+ Create Project` as its first entry. When selected (or when no project is active), display existing registered projects in the left panel and the Add Project form in the right main panel.
3. Server working directory context: Return `cwd` from `/api/projects` and display it in the Add Project panel so users clearly see which directory relative project paths resolve against.
4. Project workflow trigger: When an existing project is selected, update the sidebar action button to `⚡ [project name]` and reveal the COMMANDS and "Artifacts in Project" sections.
5. Command categories refactoring: Eliminate the `OPERATIONS` category; reassign `import` and `force-unlock` to `Plan & Apply`, and reassign `version` to `Inspection`. Rename the sidebar artifacts section to "Artifacts in Project" (listing both project and global artifacts).
6. Artifacts tab switching: Selecting the top `ARTIFACTS` tab jumps directly to the full Artifacts Library management panel.
7. Verification: Full vitest suite, Go tests, vet, and live Playwright verification.

**Boundary.** Scope is restricted to Web UI rendering, component state, project/artifact switching, and project API metadata in the local GUI server.

**Outcome.** M99 completed and verified (1 review iteration).
````

